 - regarding the #Metrics# and the #Window#:
    #Metrics# gather information about the total working time
    #Window# gathers infos about 60s price, volume and volatility changes

 - #volatility#: here we take the #volatility of returns#
    i.e. ri = (P(i) - P(i-1))/P(i-1) - % change of the investment.
    volatility is calculated over the sqrt(variance of returns)

 - #metrics# as monitor: in order to prevent race condition we synchronize all threads with #metrics# as shared monitor

 - double can store 64b values and float only 32b!!!

 - #SQL# is used here to store and handle historical data, i.e. data that should be kept after the application is stopped

 - phase 6 requires #SpringBoot# - build.gradle defines its presence in the project

    6A - Rest One-Time Requests:
    #SpringBoot# scans the package and its sub-packages for classes with bean-annotations (@...)
    it later creates required beans for the constructors of the main classes and automatically injects them there
    e.g. @RestController needs a DatabaseClient bean. DB is marked with @Repository -> it will be created
    and automatically put into the @RestController's constructor when #SpringBoot# automatically
    creates this class
    TLDR - #SpringBoot# automatizes creation and injection of instances in the constructors and execution of applications

    6B - SSE Continuous Live-Updates:
    #SSE# - SpringBoot object that is responsible for one client connection, e.g. one open tab in browser
    #LiveController# is REST-control class for SSE that opens a connection with subscribe()
    -> #LiveEventPublisher# is a SB bean that automatically publishes new events when they arrive with publish...()
    -> from Application it is injected into Logger and EventProcessor